{"title":"Conference Report: WorldCALL2023","link":"https://iafor.org/conference-report-worldcall2023/","date":1701756711000,"content":"<img width=\"150\" height=\"150\" src=\"https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/WorldCALL2023-hq-1_1500-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Conference Report: WorldCALL2023 – CALL in Critical Times\" srcset=\"https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/WorldCALL2023-hq-1_1500-150x150.jpg 150w, https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/WorldCALL2023-hq-1_1500-600x600.jpg 600w, https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/WorldCALL2023-hq-1_1500-100x100.jpg 100w, https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/WorldCALL2023-hq-1_1500-50x50.jpg 50w, https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/WorldCALL2023-hq-1_1500-300x300.jpg 300w, https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/WorldCALL2023-hq-1_1500-32x32.jpg 32w\" />In November of this year, IAFOR hosted WorldCALL2023 – CALL in Critical Times in Chiang Mai, Thailand, bringing together 100 onsite delegates and over 50 virtual participants for meaningful dialogue onComputer-Assisted Language Learning (CALL). WorldCALL2023 began with an invigorating first day dedicated to workshops. The morning session offered insights into developing effective language learning materials, <a href=\"https://iafor.org/conference-report-worldcall2023/\">...</a>\n<p><a href=\"https://iafor.org/conference-report-worldcall2023/\">Source</a></p>","author":"IAFOR","siteTitle":"The International Academic Forum (IAFOR)","siteHash":"db6175d8277e1d8dd86d5cc607b1dd9335cce255aa7e00b46d0931f23a0d47f6","entryHash":"5d32fe5f2474464ea0f576f015815e48a4bc38fb00a75d91ef4d12ffc31add60","category":"Interdisciplinary"}